{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1  \nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS DECEPTIVELY SIMPLE, BUT IT LACKS THE NECESSARY CONTEXTUAL FRAMEWORK TO BE ETHICALLY OR LEGALLY SOUND. IT IMPLIES A SUBJECTIVE, INDIVIDUALISTIC STANDARD FOR DISREGARDING LAWS, WHICH COULD UNDERMINE THE FOUNDATION OF CIVIL ORDER. LAWS ARE NOT MERELY MORAL ARTIFACTS; THEY ARE INSTITUTIONALIZED NORMS THAT EXIST TO MAINTAIN STABILITY, EVEN WHEN IMPERFECT. IF EVERY CITIZEN DECIDED BASED ON PERSONAL JUDGMENT THAT A LAW WAS \"BAD,\" CHAOS WOULD LIKELY FOLLOW, AS THERE IS NO UNIVERSAL METRIC FOR WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW. THIS STATEMENT IGNORES THE ROLE OF CIVIC DISOBEDIENCE AS A COLLECTIVE, NONVIOLENT, AND ACCOUNTABLE PRACTICE—NOT A PRIVATE DECISION.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2  \nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE FAILS TO ADDRESS THE MECHANISMS FOR CHANGING BAD LAWS, REDUCING THE COMPLEX PROCESS OF LEGISLATIVE REFORM TO A CALL FOR INDIVIDUAL DEFANCE. IT SUGGESTS THAT NONCOMPLIANCE IS THE PRIMARY OR ONLY RESPONSE TO UNJUST LAWS, WHEN IN FACT HISTORICAL CHANGE HAS USUALLY COME THROUGH PETITION, PROTEST, LITIGATION, AND ELECTIONS—NOT BLIND REBELLION. THE PHRASING ALSO LACKS ANY NOTION OF RESPONSIBILITY OR CONSEQUENCE, WHICH IS ESSENTIAL IN ANY ETHICAL DISCUSSION OF LAW AND MORALITY. WITHOUT ACKNOWLEDGING THE POTENTIAL HARM TO OTHERS OR TO THE SOCIAL CONTRACT, THE SENTENCE BECOMES A DANGEROUSLY ABSTRACT MANTRA THAT COULD BE MISUSED TO JUSTIFY SELF-SERVING DISREGARD FOR RULES THAT PROTECT THE COMMON GOOD.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -1.6093124941107817e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -2.1576648578047752e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "  \n", "logprob": -0.0059441933408379555}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.007676506415009499}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -